      "snippet": "There have been questions about why the &#x2F;ask page (<a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;ask\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;ask</a>) was running dry of Ask HNs - e.g.:<p><i>Ask HN: Why is Ask HN only showing me 14 posts?</i> - <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=49984484\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=49984484</a> - Oct 2026 (47 comments)<p><i>Ask HN: Why is pagination gone on &quot;Ask HN&quot;, and showing only 19 items?</i> - <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=50280719\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;item?id=50280719</a> - Oct 2026 (3 comments)<p>I believe I found the problem. The pool of stories for <a href=\"https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;ask\">https:&#x2F;&#x2F;news.ycombinator.com&#x2F;ask</a> has traditionally been drawn from the ranked stories list f",
