    {
      "source": "hn",
      "title": "Show HN: Synth Patch Hero",
      "url": "https://swarkentin.github.io/synth-patch-hero/",
      "author": "kaidon",
      "external_id": "50623232",
      "summary": null,
      "why_read": null,
      "authors": [],
      "category": null,
      "published": "2026-11-24T03:24:22Z",
      "score": 115,
      "comments": 23,
      "hn_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50623232",
      "snippet": "I wanted to be more deliberate and systematic in how I approach working on synth patches. With the help of our friend Claude, I put together a game that runs through exercises that builds that muscle in a fun and approachable way where you learn as you build patches on a modular rack.<p>I do not have a Eurorack, nor a strong desire to own one (yet); but I do have a bit of other physical gear. I wanted to see if the lessons would translate to boxes, where sound is also better than the browser. So I have started adding groove box specific enhanced lessons (so far just a couple for the Digitone II, but they worked so far).<p>Also:\n- You can set up MIDI in settings and play your patch in the browser with a MIDI keyboard (Chrome worked, but Safari didn&#x27;t when I tried).\n- The Help in the exercises can unblock you when you get stuck and teach you as it helps.\n- You can pick a groove box in",
      "links": []
    },
